    <description>
      <Value><![CDATA[{
  "blocks": {
    "contentData": [],
    "settingsData": [],
    "expose": [],
    "Layout": {}
  },
  "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EStreet furniture \u003Cstrong\u003Eshould \u003C/strong\u003Ebe thoughtfully designed and provided at a level that meets the functional and amenity needs of all users, whilst avoiding unnecessary visual or physical clutter. Items \u003Cstrong\u003Eshould \u003C/strong\u003Econtribute positively to the accessibility, safety, and character of the public realm. The following principles \u003Cstrong\u003Eshould \u003C/strong\u003Eguide the design and placement of street furniture: \u003C/p\u003E\u003Cul\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003Eselect high-quality, robust materials that complement the local character and require minimal maintenance \u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003Ewhere appropriate, consider dual-purpose furniture (such as integrated lighting with signage, cctv) to maximise function without overloading the streetscape \u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003Edesign and locate furniture to be usable by all, including disabled people, older adults, and those with visual impairments - avoid creating trip hazards or pinch points \u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003Eposition street furniture consistently and logically in a \u2018furniture zone\u2019, aligning lighting columns, tree pits, and utilities to create a unified and orderly streetscape \u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003Cli\u003E\u003Cp\u003Eensure clear, continuous routes for pedestrians and cyclists are maintained, avoiding obstruction from furniture, signage, or other fixed objects\u003C/p\u003E\u003C/li\u003E\u003C/ul\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003C/p\u003E"
}]]></Value>
    </description>
